Place a PKCS#12 (.pfx) certificate file named `SessionCertificate.pfx` next to this file.

The OIM API Server uses this certificate to sign session tokens. Without it the
container enters an infinite startup loop.

Generate a self-signed certificate for local/dev use:

    openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout key.pem -out cert.pem \
        -days 3650 -nodes -subj "/CN=oim-apiserver"
    openssl pkcs12 -export -out SessionCertificate.pfx \
        -inkey key.pem -in cert.pem -passout pass:

For production: use a certificate issued by your internal CA.
